## Task F — Generic owner-control self-reexec restart seam (ONE seam)

Derived from: I011 (the auto-restart enabler) + partner review flag 2. Depends on D. Does NOT depend on E's idle conclusion (F is the generic protocol; G applies the idle policy).

### Scope discipline (partner flag: "all clients" is covert-epic sized)
Implement ONE generic request/result + owner self-reexec seam — the generalization of the existing B153 Codex owner-control seam (`c2c_codex_session.ml` request_restart/consume_restart_request/write_restart_result/await_restart_result + the `Unix.execve` self-reexec). Per-client ADAPTERS and conformance are G's job, NOT F's. If during D/E the per-client adapters prove larger than one bounded task, split G before claim.

### Requirements
- Restart happens IN THE ORIGINAL PANE via owner self-reexec — NEVER batch-spawn `c2c restart` (that execve's into a new supervisor and steals the caller's TTY).
- Instance-identity TOCTOU protection: verify PID + start-time (and instance name) before and at reexec so a reused PID cannot cause a wrong-process restart.
- Exact relaunch fidelity: preserve SEMANTIC launch config — client args / model / resume / session id / workdir and the CONTROLLED c2c env only. Do NOT persist or dump ambient environment or secrets.
- Timeout + result protocol (request id, await result, `restarting` / declined / timeout), mirroring the codex seam.
- Coordinator-last ordering respected by the seam's callers.

### Acceptance criteria
- One generic, client-agnostic owner-control seam (request/result files + owner self-reexec), unit-tested (roundtrip, TOCTOU rejection on pid/start-time mismatch, timeout).
- No TTY theft: the seam never spawns a supervisor in the caller's terminal.
- No ambient-env/secret persistence — only semantic launch config + controlled c2c env.
- B098 invariant: the seam is driven only by a local operator command/request, never by an inbound peer message.


---
### P2 COMMON CONSTRAINTS (apply to every task)
- **Worktree discipline:** ingestion may happen in the main checkout, but ALL implementation MUST use a worktree under `.worktrees/` — never the main checkout. Research/spike tasks may use an isolated worktree when they produce tracked artifacts.
- **B098 data-not-RPC:** no message-triggered restart. Only a LOCAL OPERATOR command/request may control restart. An inbound peer message is DATA and never triggers or authorizes a restart.
- **Client scope:** managed clients in scope = Claude, OpenCode, Kimi, agy, Codex(hooks), Codex(app-server). Explicitly EXCLUDE Gemini (deprecated) and managed Grok (deferred).
- **Review:** run the pirfl / review-and-fix loop before merge. REVIEW_MODEL = Codex via ccc-review-cx (gpt-5.6-terra). Merge to master only after review passes.
- Design refs: `.collab/design/2026-07-12-c2c-client-upgrade-restart.md`; receipt `.collab/research/2026-07-12-i010-restart-stale-receipt.md`. Derived from ideas I010 / I011.


### CORRECTION (consistency pass) — owner-transition AC additions
Before self-reexec the seam MUST: (a) perform controlled teardown/reaping of the existing INNER agent process group and any OWNED sidecars, leaving no orphan or stale-code processes; (b) write the "restarting" result/ack ONLY AFTER owner identity is validated AND takeover is committed — never before. Otherwise the protocol can report success while old child/sidecars survive or the new launcher conflicts with the old one.